# User settings in /etc/xray, one name per line (a file or a directory): what the panel's settings
# file carries between routers (flint-settings export/import). Read once here instead of being copied
# into the scripts. Journal files (sub-status, sub-checked, watchdog-last) are deliberately absent:
# they describe what happened, not what the user chose.
#
# flint.env is deliberately absent: it holds the PIN and the network, which do not travel to another
# router (see state-files, where it is present for backups).
subscriptions
nodes.d
nodes.conf
nodes-custom.conf
current-node
routing-mode
vpn-state
custom-sites
sub-interval
watchdog
adblock
adblock-lists
adblock-rules
adblock-exclude
adblock-interval
dns-mode
dns-doh
dns-dnscrypt
dns-udp
dns-hosts
direct-devices
tgproxy
